{"text": "2026-03-27 13:48:10.746 | INFO     | trpg_py.agent.planner:plan:202 - planner round started\n", "record": {"elapsed": {"repr": "0:00:01.181855", "seconds": 1.181855}, "exception": null, "extra": {"planner_run_id": "cfdbcdf4b5e8", "planner_thread_id": "-", "planner_round": "1", "planner_input_mode": "prompt", "planner_event": "round_start", "planner_round_index": 1, "planner_input_snapshot": {"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Plan the DM instruction into a TaskDocument for the TRPG engine.\n\nA valid TaskDocument is an execution DSL. It is not a natural-language plan.\n\nTaskDocument minimal shape:\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"string\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"policy\": {},\n  \"context\": {},\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"string\",\n      \"type\": \"select|check|damage|heal|resource|effect|state\",\n      \"kind\": \"depends on type\",\n      \"args\": {},\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"when\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nAllowed type/kind pairs:\n- select: target | area | filtered\n- check: attack | save | ability | skill\n- damage: apply\n- heal: apply\n- resource: consume\n- effect: add | remove\n- state: set | adjust\n\nReference rules:\n- Use {\"$ref\": \"context.foo\"}, {\"$ref\": \"state.actors.hero_1.ac\"}, or {\"$ref\": \"result.attack_roll.outcome\"}.\n- A step may only reference results from earlier steps.\n- Use \"when\" for conditional execution.\n\nPath semantics:\n- list and read use bare store paths such as actors.goblin_1.ac, actors.aldera.hp, or actors.goblin_1.attacks.scimitar.to_hit.\n- Do not pass state.actors.goblin_1.ac directly to list or read.\n- TaskDocument $ref values keep engine namespaces, so the matching reference form is state.actors.goblin_1.ac.\n- Think of this as: tool path actors.goblin_1.ac -> TaskDocument $ref state.actors.goblin_1.ac.\n\nTool responsibilities:\n- Use search for rule evidence.\n- Use list to discover candidate bare store paths.\n- Use read to confirm the current values on a small set of candidate bare store paths, such as actor ids, AC, HP, resources, or spell slots.\n- When list or read returns `status=no_match` with suggestions, prefer those suggested paths or prefixes before retrying a nearby request.\n- Use lint to validate a candidate TaskDocument before returning status ready.\n\nDnD5e attack reminder:\n- Do not treat a natural 20 attack as an ordinary success if the plan can preserve nat semantics.\n- Prefer `check.attack` with `tags=[\"nat\"]` so the engine can emit `crit_success` or `crit_fail`.\n- When a follo...<truncated>"}]}, "planner_validation_feedback": null}, "file": {"name": "planner.py", "path": "/home/naifen/code/trpg-py/trpg_py/agent/planner.py"}, "function": "plan", "level": {"icon": "ℹ️", "name": "INFO", "no": 20}, "line": 202, "message": "planner round started", "module": "planner", "name": "trpg_py.agent.planner", "process": {"id": 5, "name": "MainProcess"}, "thread": {"id": 123431077406528, "name": "MainThread"}, "time": {"repr": "2026-03-27 13:48:10.746256+08:00", "timestamp": 1774590490.746256}}}
